1
00:00:00,073 --> 00:00:02,643
another database index gotcha is

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:03,803
that in MySQL,

3
00:00:04,103 --> 00:00:06,013
when you add a foreign key, the database

4
00:00:06,013 --> 00:00:08,833
creates an index on that column for you

5
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:10,943
automatically, if there isn't one already

6
00:00:10,999 --> 00:00:12,643
in PostgreSQL, it doesn't

7
00:00:12,643 --> 00:00:14,023
so if you're on Postgres,

8
00:00:14,193 --> 00:00:16,263
or you've moved from MySQL to Postgres, you

9
00:00:16,263 --> 00:00:18,303
have to check and confirm that your foreign

10
00:00:18,303 --> 00:00:18,783
key

11
00:00:18,953 --> 00:00:20,513
columns actually have indexes

12
00:00:20,593 --> 00:00:23,075
and it's one of the common reasons why joins

13
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:24,233
suddenly get slow
